  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Media safety initiative - Promoting safer working conditions for journalists in Uganda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;Strengthening journalists&#xBF; skills, supporting selected media organisations, and engaging key stakeholders to promote a secure environment conducive to objective, conflict-sensitive journalism. Key activities include capacity-building in conflict-sensitive and election reporting, tailored multi-dimensional safety training, provision of safety equipment, and development of structured safety protocols in collaboration with media managers. The action also addresses journalists&#xBF; mental health and wellbeing, encourages peer learning among media professionals, and promotes dialogue and awareness among security and justice actors about the importance of media safety and journalist protection. This action aims to embed safety protocols, capacity-building, and multi-stakeholder collaboration into ongoing initiatives to ensure long-term sustainability and resilience of Uganda&#xBF;s media landscape.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
